    {
      "id": "claim_aed5ab74da604166b7e9f9723dd77403",
      "statement": "tests/test_client.py covers the outbound half over MemoryTransport: start_friendship through delegate_task yields a completed booking whose detail comes from server B's injected executor with the task recorded on both sides; an empty local permission matrix makes the client's deny-by-default outbound guard raise PermissionDeniedError before any envelope is sent; and refresh_endpoint raises DiscoveryError when the well-known manifest fingerprint differs from the recorded friend while updating the stored endpoint when it matches (both via a monkeypatched _fetch_json).",
