    {
      "id": "claim_b05fb00b86684f619da9d33dc95c9fc5",
      "statement": "tests/test_policy.py pins roles and the policy engine in isolation: the five built-in roles (guest, client, partner, family, admin) with deny-by-default semantics (guest has no task:delegate, only admin has exec:terminal), a user roles.json role that extends a built-in and overrides rate limits, resolve_role raising ValueError for unknown roles, and RequestPolicy.evaluate decisions — default queue, fingerprint and speciality auto-approve rules with max_role capping (an admin rule capped down to client), and default deny.",
