    {
      "id": "claim_c1704903b617447994ee745a4da98afe",
      "statement": "tests/test_policy.py pins the three friend_request policy branches through the server: queued requests stay pending_in, notify the injected notifier with an actionable card carrying how_to_approve, and reply with pending_human True; auto-approval replies friend_accept carrying granted_role and the exact role permission matrix (client grants task:submit, no file:write) and lands as accepted; a deny-default policy replies an error envelope with FRIEND_REQUEST_DENIED and leaves no directory record; ConsoleNotifier prints the human card; and directory.approve seeded from resolve_role matches the CLI role-template approval path including the client role's task_request capacity of 5.",
