    {
      "id": "claim_287a211c979b4620af3ac7aa6be43b2b",
      "statement": "tests/test_registry.py pins two-phase proof-of-endpoint registration over live loopback HTTP (POST /register validates the signed manifest and fingerprint-to-key binding and issues a challenge_nonce; POST /register/complete with the nonce signed by the private key lists the agent, which then appears in /search and /agents/{fingerprint}) plus the rejection and lifecycle paths: forged manifest signatures, fingerprint/key mismatches, and endpoint proofs signed by a different key are rejected and never listed; re-registering the same fingerprint updates a single entry rather than duplicating; heartbeat renews entries while silence past the entry_ttl expires them; and search matches capability and free text against the manifest.",
