    {
      "id": "claim_e5e43a0b965c456eb779a91a014056e4",
      "statement": "For extension tests the bootstrap rule matters: hello, challenge, friend_request, service_search, service_book, service_cancel and service_quote are the only message types whose sender public key may come from the payload when the receiver does not know the sender, and the declared key must hash to the claimed fingerprint; a non-bootstrap message from an unknown sender fails verification with BAD_SIGNATURE, so new-flow tests either embed public_key_b64 for bootstrap types or register_known/approve the sender first.",
